# 3. compose_flip.rs, fn real_core:
#    a. the `snapshots:` field of the session deps. This REPLACES item 1 of g75-fu-engine-live.wire: `EngineTurnSnapshots` goes OUTERMOST,
#       because the actor calls `turn_aborted` on `SessionDeps.snapshots` and `SettlingSavedLogins` does not forward it:
#
#          snapshots: Arc::new(crate::compose_browser_engine::EngineTurnSnapshots::new(
#              Arc::new(SettlingSavedLogins::new({ <the worktree_snapshots block, unchanged> }, saved_login_turns.clone())),
#              engine.clone(),
#          )),
#
#    b. `owned_shells` (the `match &computer_pool { ... }` that builds the `Arc<dyn OwnedShells>`): wrap the result so a release of a
#       session reaches the engine:
#
#          let owned_shells: Arc<dyn OwnedShells> = Arc::new(crate::compose_browser_engine::EngineSessionRelease::new(owned_shells, engine.clone()));
#
#       (placed right after the existing `let owned_shells = match ... ;`; `engine` is built earlier in the same function.)
#    c. the engine host commands carry the `browser_timing` row of a command (a failed one too, with the timing of the part that ran):
#       `browser_timing` is moved into `browser_channel`; clone it there (`match browser_timing.clone() {`) and where
#       `EngineHostCommands::new(browser_channel, engine.clone(), b.host.clone())` is built use
#
#          match browser_timing {
#              Some(timing) => mixdog_tools::desktop::browser_engine::EngineHostCommands::with_timing(browser_channel, engine.clone(), b.host.clone(), timing),
#              None => mixdog_tools::desktop::browser_engine::EngineHostCommands::new(browser_channel, engine.clone(), b.host.clone()),
#          }
#
# 4. NOT done, assigned (checked): `BrowserApprovalContext::session_gate` (compose_browser_engine.rs) still answers None. A card is an
#    `ApprovalAsk` resolved through `Ctl::Approval { turn, .. }` of the session actor (RunPort), which answers `Cancelled` when its turn is
#    not the active run, so a bridge command (no tool call, no core run for a session the Node runtime hosts) has no gate to bind in the
#    tree today: the ApprovalGate implementations are RunPort (per run), HeldApprovals (a run's held request), WaitingApprovals and the
#    test gates. A session-level ask that the actor accepts without a run, or a gate the bridge borrows from the desktop connection that
#    sent the command, must exist before the desktop's bridge is pointed at browser/bridge/run: owner s4-bridge-forward (G10), which
#    already owns that re-pointing. The rest of the bridge's approval rules are in mixdog-tools and need no wiring beyond item 3 of
#    s4-bridge-core.wire: an operator `confirm` of an unattended run now always raises its card through the one path in every session, and
#    "Allow for this session" is offered and stored under the `session_life` the command carries.
#
# 5. No SERVICE_PENDING change (`host/browser/revision` is a request the core sends the desktop). No Cargo edge: the tools crate already
#    depends on mixdog-browser-engine and mixdog-core-api (HostError, CoreError); the daemon on mixdog-core-session.
